WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:06.012
Applying for jobs means the same forms, over and over. Same CV. Same answers. Every single time.

2
00:00:06.412 --> 00:00:11.488
So let Claude do it for you. You set it up once, in about thirty to forty-five minutes.

3
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:19.480
Step one. Subscribe to Claude. Pro is plenty to start, and you enter the payment yourself.

4
00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:26.630
Step two. Download the Claude app, open it, and sign in with that same account.

5
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.530
Step three. Add Claude to Chrome. Then sign in to LinkedIn and your other job sites.

6
00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:44.404
Step four. Grab the kit from the guide. No GitHub needed. Unzip it, and put the jobsearch folder on your desktop.

7
00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:51.485
Step five. Drop your CVs into the cv folder. They never leave your computer.

8
00:00:54.420 --> 00:01:02.140
Step six. In the Code tab, open your jobsearch folder, and type: set me up. Claude asks a few questions, and saves your answers.

9
00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:14.207
Step seven. Type: apply for jobs. Claude finds them, shows you a shortlist, and only applies once you say OK. Every result goes in the log.

10
00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:22.987
That's it. The full guide is at this link. You handle passwords and payment. Claude does the rest.
